    isbefore: []  # 2c83
    duplicate_of: []  # 2c83
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2c83
    pr_ref:  # 2c83
    description: "Filed by ADR-0050 (io-boundary axis) as a DISCLOSED NEGATIVE of that PR, and it\napplies to all four declared axes, not just the new one.\n\nTHE FACT. axis_drift.iter_axis_set_assignments collects module-level assignments\nwhose value is an ast.Set literal or frozenset({...}) / frozenset([...]) /\nfrozenset((...)) of STRING CONSTANTS, and whose target name contains the filter\nsubstring. Everything else is invisible to it:\n\n  * frozenset(A + B) built from other names. KNOWN_IO_BOUNDARIES was exactly\n    this shape before ADR-0050 derived it, so the linter never saw the\n    vocabulary's own headline constant.\n  * a bare tuple. CATALOG_BOUNDARY_TYPES was exactly this shape.\n  * a frozenset(SOMEDICT.values()). _READ_BOUNDARY_VALUES is exactly this.\n  * a dict keyed or valued by axis values. taint.AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP,\n    io_boundary.DEFERRED_CROSSING_SHADOWS and\n    io_boundary._READ_TARGET_KIND_BOUNDARY are all this shape, and all three\n    branch on the io-boundary vocabulary.\n  * a set whose elements are NAME references rather than string literals\n    (all_strings goes False and the whole assignment is dropped).\n    VALID_BOUNDARY_RULINGS is this shape.\n\nMEASURED CONSEQUENCE ON THE NEW AXIS: after ADR-0050 made io_boundary.py derive\nits five constants from the registry, the BOUNDAR-filtered scan collects ZERO\nassignments across packages/, scripts/ and .agent/. The linter exits 0 over an\nempty collection and would exit 0 identically if it were broken. ADR-0050\nhandles that by proving non-vacuity against a synthetic tree\n(test_the_drift_scanner_actually_fires) and by asserting the three dict\nconsumers explicitly, but those are per-axis workarounds for a shared-machinery\ngap.\n\nWHY IT WAS NOT FIXED IN THAT PR: axis_drift is shared by edge-type, symbol-kind\nand evidence-type. Widening the collector will very likely surface pre-existing\noffenders in those three vocabularies, and folding an unknown-size cleanup into\nan axis-declaration PR is how a declaration turns into a migration.\n\nSCOPE. Widen iter_axis_set_assignments to also collect ast.Tuple / ast.List\nvalues, ast.Dict keys and values, and to resolve simple module-local NAME\nreferences to already-seen string constants. Each widening is independently\nswitchable so the blast radius can be measured one at a time.\n\nFIRST STEP, AND DO NOT SKIP IT: run each widening in REPORT-ONLY mode across all\nfour axes and count new offenders BEFORE changing any gate. A widening that\nturns four green linters red on landing is correct behaviour and a bad landing;\nthe per-axis residue wants filing, not fixing in this item."  # 2c83
    fields: {}  # 2c83
