- op: discuss  # ef09
  at: '2026-09-02T00:42:27Z'  # ef09
  by: agent  # ef09
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ef09
  clock: 3  # ef09
  nonce: ef09  # ef09
  message: "FIRST STEP DONE AS FILED -- every widening run in REPORT-ONLY mode across all\nfour axes BEFORE any gate changed. The report corrected the item's own\ndiagnosis in two places, so it is recorded before the fix.\n\nREPORT-ONLY YIELD (assignments newly collected / of those, carrying values\nabsent from that axis's registry):\n\n  axis            +tuple,list   +dict-keys   +dict-VALUES   +NAME refs   ALL\n  edge-type          0            3 / 0         0             0          3 / 0\n  evidence-type      0            0             0             0          0\n  io-boundary        0            1 / 2         1 / 0         0          1 / 2\n  symbol-kind        3 / 13       5 / 8         3 / 5         0          9 / 26\n\nCORRECTION 1 -- THE THREE WIDENINGS DO NOT RESTORE io-boundary NON-VACUITY,\nwhich is what this item was filed to do. After all three, the BOUNDAR scan\ncollects exactly ONE assignment. The five constants the item names are\ninvisible for THREE different reasons it did not separate:\n  * KNOWN_IO_BOUNDARIES, CATALOG_BOUNDARY_TYPES and _READ_BOUNDARY_VALUES are\n    now produced by a CALL (all_io_boundary_names(), catalog_declarable_names(),\n    frozenset(SOMEDICT.values())). No widening in this item's scope reaches a\n    call -- AND IT SHOULD NOT: a constant DERIVED from the registry cannot\n    drift from it. There is nothing there for a drift linter to check. The\n    vacuity ADR-0050 disclosed is therefore not a collector gap; it is the\n    correct consequence of deriving the constants, and the synthetic-offender\n    test is the right answer to it, not a widening.\n  * AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP (taint.py:1540) and DEFERRED_CROSSING_SHADOWS\n    (io_boundary.py:196) are invisible because neither NAME contains\n    \"BOUNDAR\" -- they fail the NAME FILTER, not the shape test. Widening the\n    collector will never reach them. FILED SEPARATELY as a distinct defect;\n    this item cannot fix it.\n  * VALID_BOUNDARY_RULINGS is reached by the NAME-ref widening (it resolves\n    to call_site_undecidable / unruled) and is then correctly excluded by\n    name, being the boundary-RULING vocabulary. Worth noting that ADR-0050\n    disclosed this exclusion as DEAD; the widening makes it load-bearing.\n\nCORRECTION 2 -- \"+NAME refs\" YIELDS ZERO NEW OFFENDERS ON ALL FOUR AXES. It is\nimplemented because VALID_BOUNDARY_RULINGS is genuinely that shape and a\nfuture set will be, but nobody should expect it to find anything today.\n(An instrument bug found en route: the first cut of the resolver read only\nast.Assign, missing every ``NAME: Final[str] = \"...\"`` -- which is the house\nstyle for exactly these constants. It reported 0 for the right answer by the\nwrong route until fixed.)\n\nWHAT LANDED. iter_axis_set_assignments now collects bare tuples/lists, dict\nKEYS and dict VALUES, and module-local NAME references. A dict with strings\non BOTH sides yields <NAME>:keys and <NAME>:values SEPARATELY -- forced by\nio_boundary._READ_TARGET_KIND_BOUNDARY, which is keyed by io_target_kind\nvalues and valued by io-boundary names, two axes in one assignment. Unioning\nthe sides would make io-boundary exclude the whole constant to silence the\nkeys, losing the check on the values. A bare-name exclusion still silences\nboth sides, so every pre-existing exclusion keeps its meaning.\n\nRESIDUE, CLASSIFIED INDIVIDUALLY RATHER THAN BULK-STAMPED. Five of the six\nnewly-red constants are axis-name collisions, and the test that separates a\ncollision from a consumer is CONFORMANCE RATIO -- each is 0/N conformant with\nthe registry whose substring it matched:\n  _RELATED_ENDPOINT_KINDS   a meta[\"framework_role\"] vocabulary; ADR-0027\n                            Phase 3 folded these OFF Symbol.kind and\n                            cmd_routes reads meta.framework_role first\n                            (cli.py:2239). NOT the fossil it first looked\n                            like -- checked before claiming.\n  _PROVENANCE_KINDS         catalogue provenance categories\n  _ANNOTATION_KINDS         tracker TUI annotation shapes\n  _READ_TARGET_KIND_BOUNDARY  cross-axis map (see above)\n  _PHP_CONTAINER_KINDS:keys  tree-sitter NODE types; its VALUES are real\n                            Symbol.kinds and REMAIN CHECKED\nTHE SIXTH IS A REAL FINDING, filed as INV-lagot: scip/index.py:94 _KIND_MAP\nis a genuine Symbol.kind consumer -- 5 of its 8 values ARE registered -- and\nthe other three (parameter, type_parameter, meta) plus the \"unknown\" fallback\nat index.py:166 are phantom values. Suppressed with an exclusion that says so\nin as many words and names the item to delete it with, per this item's own\ninstruction that per-axis residue is filed rather than fixed.\n\nNON-VACUITY PROVEN, not assumed: a planted offender in each newly-collected\nshape (tuple, dict key, NAME ref) is asserted to be REPORTED through\nfind_drift, and a separate test asserts that excluding NAME:keys leaves\nNAME:values still reported -- the degradation that would otherwise turn the\nside split back into a whole-constant exclusion with nothing failing.\n\nSHIPPED as dev 882e1206d5. VERIFIED ON THE MERGED TREE: all four drift\nlinters exit 0 (check-edge-type-drift, check-evidence-type-drift,\ncheck-symbol-kind-drift, check-io-boundary-drift), and a planted dict\noffender against a synthetic registry IS reported --\n\"packages/d/src/x.py:1 (_FOO_EDGE_TYPE_W): contains ['phantom_dict_value']\nnot in canonical registry\" -- so the widened collector is non-vacuous rather\nthan merely green. 6244 tests pass, 100% coverage on changed files."  # ef09
